      "Before you raise a hand in class, write the problem number and copy the last correct line. Underline the command word if there is one. Circle the unit. If you are in a literature lesson, mark the sentence in the extract you cannot paraphrase. If you are in science, name the process and the stage: I can write the word equation but I cannot say why the temperature must be high. Precision lets the teacher aim. Aiming is what a lesson can afford.",
      "Do the waiting work. Attempt the question for a fixed time — five minutes is enough — so you are not asking for a tour of a path you have not stepped on. Teachers reasonably protect class time from students who have not opened the book. An attempt also shows you which part is actually hard. Often the hard part is not the whole topic. It is a fraction, a negative sign, or a word like hence that you skipped.",
      "## The stuck step on paper",
      "Choose the moment. A question that helps twelve other people belongs in the lesson. A question that is only your missing homework belongs after the bell or in the next extra class. Interrupting a demonstration to confess that you did not copy yesterday's notes wastes a demonstration. Write the private question in the margin and catch the teacher at the door with the page already open. Open pages get answers. Closed bags get later.",
