      "Do not outsource the whole subject to one conversation. One conversation can fix a method. It cannot replace a week of practice. After the teacher shows the step, do a similar question immediately, in the lesson if there is time, or that evening. If you cannot repeat the step without looking, you did not receive an explanation. You received a performance. Performances fade by supper.",
      "Group help is different from private help. In a group, ask a question whose answer other people can use: How do we know which quantity is the subject of the formula. Private gaps — you missed three days of school — need a short appointment, not a public halt. Be honest about absence. Pretending you were present forces the teacher to reteach a scene the class has already left. Honesty lets them point you to the exact notes or the peer who writes cleanly.",
