      "Write a rough list of points in short phrases, still in your own words, before you write the paragraph. Count them against the marks and the word limit. If the question wants ten points and you have sixteen phrases, you have not yet dropped examples. Dropping is the skill. Students fear dropping because the passage seemed to love those sentences. The passage can love them. Your summary cannot afford them.",
      "Own words are not a thesaurus attack. Replacing commence with begin is fine. Replacing a simple verb with a longer verb you do not control is how meaning flips. If the passage says the committee postponed the meeting, do not write the committee cancelled the meeting unless the passage said that. Postpone and cancel are different spines. Accuracy beats decoration in summary more than in almost any other exercise.",
