      "## Blanks, units, misread",
      "First sweep: unanswered numbers. Flip every page. Circle any question number with no ink. Attempt the parts you can: a definition, a formula, a labelled diagram, a one-line plan. A part-answer can still take part-marks. A blank cannot. If two blanks remain, choose the one with more marks, not the one that feels more like your personality. Personality is not in the mark scheme.",
      "Second sweep: units and labels. In calculations, check that the final line has the unit the question named. In graphs, check axis labels and the unit in brackets. In biology diagrams, check that the label line touches the part. A correct number with no unit is a half-finished product. The last ten minutes exist for half-finished products. They do not exist for starting a new essay style.",
      "Third sweep: the question you misread. Look only at command words and constraints: not, except, two reasons, with reference to the passage, give your answer in standard form. Misreading is the most expensive error because the writing can be excellent and still be the wrong task. If you find a misread and there is time, add the missing task in the remaining space and put a clear arrow. Do not scribble over a page of working so that nothing can be marked.",
      "Candidate details belong in the sweep. A booklet without a name is a different disaster from a missing unit. Check the cover when you still have minutes, not when the invigilator is collecting.",
      "Check transferred numbers. If step two used 3.6 and the question gave 3.8, the rest may be method marks with a factual bruise, or it may be a wreck. Fixing an early copy error can rescue a whole question in one minute. This is why you should not fill every second of the paper with new sentences. One minute of arithmetic rescue can outweigh three extra lines of an already complete letter.",
      "In language papers, the sweep is different but still a sweep. Count the number of points in a summary against the question. Look at the address and closing of a letter. Check that a composition has an ending, even a short one. An unfinished story with a last line is kinder to a marker than a story that stops in a corridor. Add the last line. Then stop decorating.",
      "## Multiple-choice is a different sweep",
