      "Watch the room's clock and your own watch if you have one, because they can disagree. When the invigilator says ten minutes, believe the invigilator. Start the sweep even if you are mid-sentence. Mid-sentence can be finished in twenty seconds after the blanks are hunted. Blanks cannot be hunted after pens down. Pens down is a hard wall. Your attachment to a paragraph is not.",
      "If you finish earlier than ten minutes, do not leave the hall in your mind. Early finishers invent errors by rewriting working they already did correctly. Use extra time for the same sweeps, slower, and for your candidate details. Then sit. Sitting is part of the method. Restless rewriting is how a correct 4 becomes an incorrect 9.",
      "Multiple-choice papers need a particular sweep: unanswered bubbles, double bubbles, and questions you flagged. A flagged question should be visited before you start changing answers you were confident about. Confidence changes at the end of a paper are often fatigue wearing a costume. Fatigue likes to pick a different option because it looks fresh. Fresh is not a reason.",
      "Practise the sweep on timed past questions at home so it feels ordinary. Ordinary methods survive noise. If you never practise ending, you will only know how to continue. Continuing is the habit that wastes the last ten minutes. Put a timer at forty minutes for a fifty-minute homework paper and force the sweep. The discomfort is the lesson.",
